@UniShareProject.API_HostAddress = http://localhost:5100

### Variables for testing
@testEmail = test.user@principia.edu
@testPassword = Th1s1satest!
@testEmail2 = another.user@principia.edu
@testPassword2 = AnotherPassword123

# NOTE: Replace this with the actual token from your login response
@authToken =   eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..h24mMLTqfER2U9I2HkQXgHzA0287MpdyCVvF_Ww3Q0Y

# AUTH ENDPOINTS
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Register a new user
POST {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User",
  "email": "{{testEmail}}",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### Login with valid credentials (COPY THE TOKEN FROM THIS RESPONSE)
POST {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{testEmail}}",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### Register another user for testing
POST {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Another",
  "lastName": "User", 
  "email": "{{testEmail2}}",
  "password": "{{testPassword2}}"
}

### Login with second user (COPY THE TOKEN FROM THIS RESPONSE)
POST {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{testEmail2}}",
  "password": "{{testPassword2}}"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ITEMS ENDPOINTS (AUTHENTICATION REQUIRED)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Create a new item (REPLACE {{authToken}} WITH ACTUAL TOKEN)
POST {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/items
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "title": "Calculus Textbook",
  "description": "Like new condition calculus textbook for Math 151. No highlighting or writing inside.",
  "categoryId": 1,
  "price": 75.00,
  "conditionId": 1
}

### Create another item for testing  
POST {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/items
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "title": "MacBook Pro 2019",
  "description": "Used MacBook Pro in good condition. Some minor scratches on the back.",
  "categoryId": 2,
  "price": 899.99,
  "conditionId": 2
}

### Request purchase of an item (sets status to Pending)
POST {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/items/1/request-purchase
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Update item status (requires authentication)
PATCH {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/items/1/status?statusId=2
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ITEMS ENDPOINTS (NO AUTHENTICATION REQUIRED)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Get specific item by ID
GET {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/items/1

### Search all items (no filters)
GET {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/items

### Search items with category filter
GET {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/items?categoryId=1

### Search items with status filter
GET {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/items?statusId=1

### Search items with condition filter  
GET {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/items?conditionId=1

### Search items with text query
GET {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/items?q=textbook

### Search items with pagination
GET {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/items?page=1&pageSize=5

### Search items with multiple filters
GET {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/items?categoryId=1&statusId=1&q=calculus&page=1&pageSize=10

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ERROR SCENARIOS
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Register - Invalid email domain (should fail)
POST {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Invalid",
  "lastName": "User",
  "email": "invalid@gmail.com",
  "password": "TestPassword123"
}

### Register - Duplicate email (should fail after first registration)
POST {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Duplicate",
  "lastName": "User",
  "email": "{{testEmail}}",
  "password": "DifferentPassword123"
}

### Login with invalid credentials (should fail)
POST {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{testEmail}}",
  "password": "WrongPassword"
}

### Create item without authentication (should fail with 401)
POST {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Unauthorized Item",
  "description": "This should fail without proper auth",
  "categoryId": 1,
  "price": 50.00,
  "conditionId": 1
}

### Create item with invalid data (should fail with validation errors)
POST {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/items
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "Invalid item with empty title",
  "price": -10.00,
  "conditionId": 999
}

### Update item status without authentication (should fail)
PATCH {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/items/1/status?statusId=3

### Get non-existent item (should return 404)
GET {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/items/999999

### Request purchase without authentication (should fail with 401)
POST {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/items/1/request-purchase

### Request purchase of non-existent item (should return 404)
POST {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/items/999999/request-purchase
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Request purchase of already pending item (should return 409 Conflict)
POST {{UniShareProject.API_HostAddress}}/api/items/1/request-purchase
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TESTING INSTRUCTIONS
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 
# 1. First, run the "Register a new user" request
# 2. Then run "Login with valid credentials" 
# 3. Copy the "token" value from the login response
# 4. Replace {{authToken}} in the @authToken variable at the top with the actual token
# 5. Now you can test the authenticated endpoints
# 
# Purchase Flow Testing:
# 1. Create an item using POST /api/items
# 2. Get the item by ID to verify it's Active (statusId: 1)
# 3. Request purchase using POST /api/items/{id}/request-purchase
# 4. Get the item again to verify it's now Pending (statusId: 2)
# 5. Try to request purchase again to see 409 Conflict response
# 
# The JWT token should look like:
# eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiIxIiwibmFtZSI6IlRlc3QgVXNlciIsImVtYWlsIjoidGVzdC51c2VyQHByaW5jaXBpYS5lZHUiLCJyb2xlIjoidXNlciIsImp0aSI6IjEyMzQ1Njc4LTkwYWItY2RlZi0xMjM0LTU2Nzg5MGFiY2RlZiIsImlhdCI6IjE3MDEwMDAwMDAiLCJpc3MiOiJVbmlTaGFyZVByb2plY3QuQVBJIiwiYXVkIjoiVW5pU2hhcmVQcm9qZWN0LkNsaWVudCIsImV4cCI6MTcwMTA4NjQwMH0.SIGNATURE_PART
